       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. A visiting family and the timing of evening rounds aren't clinical reasons for a dose five times the maximum. At 50 mg daily, this patient is at real risk of profound hypotension and prolonged shock. The risk is higher because amlodipine's half-life is 30\u201350 hours, so the drug builds up over repeated doses and can't be quickly reversed.\n\nI can help in these ways:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily now**, the maximum labeled dose, if you need a high dose started today.\n- **Enter 5 mg once daily** with a plan to titrate up in 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **Add a note** to either order, such as \"titrate per BP; hold for SBP <100.\"\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than 10 mg of amlodipine, a pharmacist or cardiology consult is the safer route. They can review it and help set up monitoring. If you decide to place the order yourself through another channel, that decision is yours. I can't enter it as written.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
